.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A little helper class to quickly find all vertices in the epsilon environment of a given position\&. Construct an instance with an array of positions\&. The class stores the given positions by their indices and sorts them by their distance to an arbitrary chosen plane\&. You can then query the instance for all vertices close to a given position in an average \fBO(log n)\fP time, with \fBO(n)\fP worst case complexity when all vertices lay on the plane\&. The plane is chosen so that it avoids common planes in usual data sets\&. 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "Assimp::SpatialSort::SpatialSort ()"

.SS "Assimp::SpatialSort::SpatialSort (const \fBaiVector3D\fP * pPositions, unsigned int pNumPositions, unsigned int pElementOffset)"
Constructs a spatially sorted representation from the given position array\&. Supply the positions in its layout in memory, the class will only refer to them by index\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpPositions\fP Pointer to the first position vector of the array\&. 
.br
\fIpNumPositions\fP Number of vectors to expect in that array\&. 
.br
\fIpElementOffset\fP Offset in bytes from the beginning of one vector in memory to the beginning of the next vector\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "Assimp::SpatialSort::~SpatialSort ()"
Destructor 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::Append (const \fBaiVector3D\fP * pPositions, unsigned int pNumPositions, unsigned int pElementOffset, bool pFinalize = \fRtrue\fP)"
Same as \fBFill()\fP, except the method appends to existing data in the \fBSpatialSort\fP\&. 
.SS "\fBai_real\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::CalculateDistance (const \fBaiVector3D\fP & pPosition) const\fR [protected]\fP"
Return the distance to the sorting plane\&. 
.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::Fill (const \fBaiVector3D\fP * pPositions, unsigned int pNumPositions, unsigned int pElementOffset, bool pFinalize = \fRtrue\fP)"
Sets the input data for the \fBSpatialSort\fP\&. This replaces existing data, if any\&. The new data receives new indices in ascending order\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpPositions\fP Pointer to the first position vector of the array\&. 
.br
\fIpNumPositions\fP Number of vectors to expect in that array\&. 
.br
\fIpElementOffset\fP Offset in bytes from the beginning of one vector in memory to the beginning of the next vector\&. 
.br
\fIpFinalize\fP Specifies whether the \fBSpatialSort\fP's internal representation is finalized after the new data has been added\&. Finalization is required in order to use #FindPosition() or \fBGenerateMappingTable()\fP\&. If you don't finalize yet, you can use \fBAppend()\fP to add data from other sources\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::Finalize ()"
Finalize the spatial hash data structure\&. This can be useful after multiple calls to \fBAppend()\fP with the pFinalize parameter set to false\&. This is finally required before one of \fBFindPositions()\fP and \fBGenerateMappingTable()\fP can be called to query the spatial sort\&. 
.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::FindIdenticalPositions (const \fBaiVector3D\fP & pPosition, std::vector< unsigned int > & poResults) const"
Fills an array with indices of all positions identical to the given position\&. In opposite to \fBFindPositions()\fP, not an epsilon is used but a (very low) tolerance of four floating-point units\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpPosition\fP The position to look for vertices\&. 
.br
\fIpoResults\fP The container to store the indices of the found positions\&. Will be emptied by the call so it may contain anything\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SpatialSort::FindPositions (const \fBaiVector3D\fP & pPosition, \fBai_real\fP pRadius, std::vector< unsigned int > & poResults) const"
Returns an iterator for all positions close to the given position\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpPosition\fP The position to look for vertices\&. 
.br
\fIpRadius\fP Maximal distance from the position a vertex may have to be counted in\&. 
.br
\fIpoResults\fP The container to store the indices of the found positions\&. Will be emptied by the call so it may contain anything\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An iterator to iterate over all vertices in the given area\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "unsigned int Assimp::SpatialSort::GenerateMappingTable (std::vector< unsigned int > & fill, \fBai_real\fP pRadius) const"
Compute a table that maps each vertex ID referring to a spatially close enough position to the same output ID\&. Output IDs are assigned in ascending order from 0\&.\&.\&.n\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfill\fP Will be filled with numPositions entries\&. 
.br
\fIpRadius\fP Maximal distance from the position a vertex may have to be counted in\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Number of unique vertices (n)\&. 
.br
 
.RE
.PP

